import lib/filesystem.dl

create a temporary directory and set first to it
create a temporary directory and set second to it
print lines (first succeeded), (second succeeded) and (first's directory path is not second's directory path)

set origin to the file system entry at first's directory path
set counterpart to the file system entry at second's directory path
print line ((origin lookup succeeded) and (origin was found)) and (origin is a directory)
print line ((counterpart lookup succeeded) and (counterpart was found)) and (counterpart is a directory)

set file to formatted "{first's directory path}/payload.bin"
set payload to a new string buffer containing 5 bytes
store 65 as a byte into the data of payload at 0
store 0 as a byte into the data of payload at 1
store 66 as a byte into the data of payload at 2
store 67 as a byte into the data of payload at 3
store 68 as a byte into the data of payload at 4
write payload to the file at file and print line it succeeded

open the file at file for streaming reads
set input to it
print line input succeeded
read up to 3 bytes from input and set initial to it
print lines (initial succeeded), initial's count and (initial reached the end of file)
print lines (the character at 0 in initial's data) and (the character at 1 in initial's data)
print line (the character at 2 in initial's data)

read up to 3 bytes from input and set following to it
print lines (following succeeded), following's count and (following reached the end of file)
print lines (the character at 0 in following's data) and (the character at 1 in following's data)

read up to 3 bytes from input and set final to it
print lines (final succeeded), final's count and (final reached the end of file)

read up to (-1) bytes from input and set invalid to it
print lines (invalid succeeded), invalid's count and (invalid reached the end of file)
print line (the length of invalid's error message) > 0

open the file at "tests/required/filesystem_streaming_temp/missing.bin" for streaming reads
set missing to it
print lines (missing succeeded) and (the length of missing's error message > 0)

remove the filesystem tree at first's directory path and set purge to it
remove the filesystem tree at second's directory path and set removal to it
print lines (purge succeeded) and (removal succeeded)
